Package: twoPhaseSens
Title: Sensitivity Analysis for Covariates Observed in Two-Phase Samples
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Rophence", "Ojiambo", email = "rophence.ojiambo@nyu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6798-9066")), person("Jemar", "Bather", email = "jemar.bather@nyu.edu", role = "aut", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0285-3678")))
Description: Provides a structured method-comparison sensitivity-analysis
    workflow for linear regression when important continuous adjustment
    covariates are observed only in a Phase-2 subsample. Implements naive
    analysis, complete-case analysis, fully conditional specification multiple
    imputation, joint-model multiple imputation, inverse probability
    weighting, and augmented inverse probability weighting, with standardized
    tables, diagnostics, and publication-style forest plots.
